reverse-print.text:
Recursive linked-list output
Understand the idea
A recursive function first visits the next node and prints the current node while returning.
This can print values in reverse order without reversing the links.


Correct option
B — prints all nodes in reverse order.
It does not reverse the links.


Why
The NULL check stops recursion. Each call first processes head->next and prints its own data only after that call returns. So the last node prints first.
